    <briefdescription>
<para>Snapshot of tuning counters for tasks that passed through the queue. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Inline-mode executions are not counted. The values are sampled with relaxed atomic loads, so they are approximate while the pool is running. &quot;Relaxed&quot; means the number is read cheaply without any ordering guarantees, which is fine for a tuning gauge that nobody makes decisions from in real time. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
